## Context

This proposes replacing [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject);
that accepted record remains unchanged. The [incident correction](/kb/incidents/4471-split)
shows why subject-only merging hid the booking-v3 hint failure under the parser ticket.
The support desk must approve this proposal before it becomes policy.

## Proposed decision

Read the report and look up its tenant. Compare tenant locale, form version and
channel, using the existing `causeOf` and `sameCause` logic. Merge only reports
with the same demonstrated cause. A matching subject or intake tag alone is
insufficient. Unknown tenants and contradictory symptoms need investigation;
do not automatically merge them.

## Executable counterexamples

<DedupeExplorer />

App versus email can describe the same parser failure despite different subjects.
The same subject and tenant can describe different causes through form versus app.
The same subject and channel can describe different causes for different tenants.
Different subjects can describe the same form-hint failure. Unknown tenants are
not proven duplicates, even if both subjects match.

## Consequences

Triage costs more reading, but separate causes retain separate engineering owners,
counts and verification. Deduplicate export rows by report ID before counting.
Keep anomalous descriptions and their assigned group visible until investigated.
Review the rule against fresh exports instead of trusting an old accepted page
more than current evidence.

